<newsitem itemid="383628" id="root" date="1997-02-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: York International Q4 oper shr rises.</title>
<headline>York International Q4 oper shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>YORK, Pa. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth Qtr Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p> December 31	     1996	   1995	1996	 1995</p>
<p> Sales		    $841.4	$831.7  $3,218.5   $2,929.9</p>
<p>Income from operations</p>
<p>before amortization</p>
<p>  &amp; impairment loss     56.3	  57.2     248.3	235.5</p>
<p>Purchase accounting</p>
<p>  amortization	     2.5	   2.9	 9.9	 12.7</p>
<p> Impairment loss	    --	 244.5	  --	244.5</p>
<p>Income (loss) from</p>
<p>  Operations		53.8     (190.1)     238.4     (21.7)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	39.3     (180.4)     147.9     (96.1)</p>
<p> Shr			  0.89	(4.22)	3.37     (2.36)</p>
<p> Avg shares	     44,352	42,735    43,950     40,630</p>
<p>(in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>Full company name is York International Corp</p>
<p>NOTE: In Q4 1995, York adopted SAFS 121, a statement of financial accounting standard called &quot;Accounting for the Impairment of Long-lived Assets and for Long-lived Assets to Be Disposed Of.&quot; The adoption of this standard resulted in a $244.5 million non-cash charge to operating expenses in that quarter. Without it, Q4 1995 earnings were $0.69 per share.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
